        "description": "## Overview\n[org.apache.logging.log4j:log4j-core](https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/) is a logging library for Java.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Remote Code Execution (RCE). Apache Log4j2 JNDI features used in configuration, log messages, and parameters do not protect against attacker controlled LDAP and other JNDI related endpoints. An attacker who can control log messages or log message parameters can execute arbitrary code loaded from remote servers when message lookup substitution is enabled.\n\nThis vulnerability is also known as Log4Shell.\n\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.logging.log4j:log4j-core` to version 2.3.1, 2.12.2, 2.15.0 or higher.\n\n## References\n- [Apache Security Advisory](https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/security.html)\n- [CISA Guidance](https://www.cisa.gov/uscert/apache-log4j-vulnerability-guidance)\n",
        "from": [
