        "description": "## Overview\n[org.apache.logging.log4j:log4j-core](https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/) is a logging library for Java.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Denial of Service (DoS) and remote code execution in certain non-default configurations. The fix for CVE-2021-44228 in Log4j 2.15.0 was incomplete: when the logging configuration uses a non-default Pattern Layout with a Context Lookup, attackers with control over Thread Context Map (MDC) input data can craft malicious input using a JNDI Lookup pattern.\n\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.logging.log4j:log4j-core` to version 2.3.1, 2.12.2, 2.16.0 or higher.\n",
